{"In fetchAvailabilityAndSetCache, calling SelectedCalendarRepository.updateManyByCredentialId(this.credential.id, {}) with an empty data object {} is a no-op \u2014 Prisma's @updatedAt directive only fires when at least one field is actually being updated. The comment claims this updates SelectedCalendar.updatedAt, but the call will silently do nothing, leaving the timestamp stale": 0.9626401662826538, "scripts/test-gcal-webhooks.sh uses BSD-only sed -i '' which fails on GNU sed (Linux), breaking the script in many dev environments": 0.9431759715080261, "deleteCacheHandler throws a generic Error when the credential is missing or not owned by the user, causing tRPC to return an INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR instead of a proper NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN style error code": 0.7826616168022156, "CalendarCacheRepository is directly instantiated via new CalendarCacheRepository() instead of using the CalendarCache.init() factory, which checks the calendar-cache feature flag. When the feature is disabled globally, this code still queries the CalendarCache database table instead of returning empty results via CalendarCacheRepositoryMock": 0.9415380954742432, "updateManyByCredentialId accepts Prisma.SelectedCalendarUpdateInput (which includes nested relational operations) but passes it to updateMany(), which only accepts Prisma.SelectedCalendarUpdateManyMutationInput (scalar-only). This incorrect type signature will allow future callers to pass relational update operations that cause runtime errors": 0.9003837704658508, "In connectedCalendars.handler.ts, cacheStatusMap.get(calendar.credentialId) || null uses the || operator instead of ?? - when Map.get() returns undefined both operators return null correctly, but || would also coerce any falsy value (e.g., 0, false) to null, which is semantically incorrect for a Date | null type": 0.25417834520339966}